WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
France, 2025.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.010
About eight million immigrants live there.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.670
That's 11.6 per cent of
everyone in the country.

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.610
Back in 1999, the share
was only 7.3 per cent.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.650
And 49.2 per cent of
them were African-born.

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.230
Is that recent refugees?

7
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.250
Post-war jobs?

8
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:20.870
Tourism?

9
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.230
How did an empire help
make France so diverse?

10
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.430
In this mission, you'll
trace France's empire,

11
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:33.250
from royal colonies in 1674 to the
plantations of the Caribbean and Réunion.

12
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll follow later
moves to mainland France,

13
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.430
and test them against today's figures.

14
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.150
Your mission: explain how an empire
helped make France so diverse.
